@startuml timing-idle-event
title Idle event handshake: the slave releases DATA only after one complete clock pulse
binary "CLK" as CLK
binary "DATA" as DATA
binary "Slave drives DATA low" as S
concise "Phase" as P

@0
CLK is low
DATA is high
S is low
P is "idle"

@10
S is high
DATA is low
P is "event signal"

@20
P is "master sees DATA low"

@30
CLK is high
P is "confirmation tick"

@40
CLK is low

@42
S is low
DATA is high
P is "released"

@55
P is "master checks DATA"

@60
CLK is high
P is "START"

@65
DATA is low

@70
CLK is low
P is "master frame"

@80
DATA is low
@enduml
